Feature: Unity Catalog Schema for Sample Sales Data

  Background:
    Given a Unity Catalog schema named "purgo_playground" exists
    And a table named "sample_sales_data" is created within the schema
    And the table has the following columns:
      | Column Name | Data Type |
      | country_cd  | string    |
      | product_id  | string    |
      | qty_sold    | int       |
      | sales_date  | date      |

  Scenario: Validate data insertion into sample_sales_data table
    Given the sample data from "sample_sales_data.csv" is available
    When the data is inserted into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table
    Then the table should contain the following data:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
      | US         | P1002      | 30       | 2024-01-16  |
      | CA         | P1001      | 40       | 2024-01-15  |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |
      | UK         | P1002      | 35       | 2024-01-18  |
      | UK         | P1004      | 20       | 2024-01-19  |
      | IN         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-20  |
      | IN         | P1003      | 45       | 2024-01-21  |
      | AU         | P1004      | 55       | 2024-01-22  |
      | AU         | P1002      | 38       | 2024-01-23  |

  Scenario Outline: Validate data type and format for each column
    Given a row with <country_cd>, <product_id>, <qty_sold>, <sales_date>
    When the row is inserted into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table
    Then the data types should be validated as follows:
      | Column Name | Expected Data Type |
      | country_cd  | string             |
      | product_id  | string             |
      | qty_sold    | int                |
      | sales_date  | date               |
    And the sales_date should be in the format "YYYY-MM-DD"

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |

  Scenario: Handle error when inserting invalid data
    Given a row with country_cd as "US", product_id as "P1001", qty_sold as "fifty", sales_date as "2024-01-15"
    When the row is inserted into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table
    Then an error should occur with the message "Invalid data type for qty_sold, expected integer"

  Scenario: Ensure non-nullable constraints for country_cd and product_id
    Given a row with country_cd as null, product_id as "P1001", qty_sold as 50, sales_date as "2024-01-15"
    When the row is inserted into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table
    Then an error should occur with the message "country_cd cannot be null"

    Given a row with country_cd as "US", product_id as null, qty_sold as 50, sales_date as "2024-01-15"
    When the row is inserted into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table
    Then an error should occur with the message "product_id cannot be null"

  Scenario: Define primary key and indexing requirements
    Given the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" is created
    When defining the primary key
    Then the primary key should be a combination of "country_cd" and "product_id"
    And an index should be created on "sales_date" to optimize query performance